 "final": "STATUS: fail\nSUMMARY: The flag-off path and most flag-on criteria hold: stacked restore, pending-addition cleanup, row cells, root bounding, and the frozen install all passed. Two reproduced bugs break \"targets stay visible\". Both come from the shadow-root walk hiding siblings that sit inside a target's light-DOM subtree or flat-tree rendering.\nFILES TOUCHED: none (probe file created and deleted; `git status` matches the start: package.json, ariaHideOutside.ts, ariaHideOutside.test.js, yarn.lock)\nFINDINGS:\n- [blocking] Content inside a target is hidden. Repro: `dialog` (role=dialog, light DOM) contains host `h`; `h`'s shadow is `<input id=b><button id=c>`. `ariaHideOutside([dialog, b])` leaves `c` with `aria-hidden=\"true\"`, though `c` is inside target `dialog`. Cause: the light walk REJECTs the whole target subtree, but `walk(shadowRoot)` for the enclosing shadow root doesn't know about the outer target. The same sibling added after the call is NOT hidden (the observer guard skips it), so initial and later behavior disagree.\n- [blocking] A slotted target becomes hidden in the flat tree. Repro: host `h` with shadow `<div id=w><slot></slot></div><input id=t1>`; light child `L` of `h`; `ariaHideOutside([t1, L])`. `w` gets `aria-hidden` (it is a sibling of `t1`), and `L.assignedSlot` \u2192 `slot` \u2192 `w` is hidden. The attribute on `L` itself is clean, so this only shows up as an ancestor hidden in the flat tree. Needs two targets, so narrower than the first bug.\n- [minor] Open design gap, not probed: a shadow root of a host that only slots a light-DOM target is not walked, so its non-slotted siblings stay visible. Spec-literal reading (\"enclosing\" = target's ancestors) excludes it.\nCHECKS:\n- flag off: target in shadow, siblings and later additions untouched, body hidden as before \u2192 pass\n- [A] slotted target under a hidden wrapper (flat-tree ancestry via assignedSlot) \u2192 fail\n- [B] seeded fuzz, 1000 random light/shadow trees (depth \u22643\u20134), 1\u20133 random targets, random additions, checking aria-hidden against a model \u2192 fail at iter 0, same family as the first finding; the fuzz stopped at the first failure\n- [C] root = shadow host containing target: host, body, light sibling not hidden; shadow sibling hidden \u2192 pass\n- [D] role=row in shadow: row and cell hidden, button not \u2192 pass\n- [E] keepVisible on a shadow element added right after the call \u2192 pass (keepVisible must be imported from `../src/ariaHideOutside`; the index doesn't export it)\n- [F] nested hosts across roots (target in B, B's host inside A), additions to A / B / inside target, then cleanup restores \u2192 pass\n- [G] stacked: inner call in body, cleanup inner, add to shadow root \u2192 hidden; cleanup outer \u2192 restored \u2192 pass\n- [H] addition to shadow root followed by synchronous cleanup \u2192 not hidden \u2192 pass\n- [I] target is a shadow host: additions in its shadow and light children stay visible, other host hidden \u2192 pass\n- [J] target light dialog containing a host with target + sibling in its shadow \u2192 fail (see first finding)\n- [J2] same, with an addition in that shadow after the call \u2192 pass (inconsistent with J)\n- `yarn install --immutable --mode=skip-build` \u2192 pass; `@react-stately/flags` is 3.1.2, matching package.json\n- Not run: iframe-owned root, `shouldUseInert` in shadow (jsdom may lack `inert`), react-aria-components Popover/Modal inside a shadow root\nOPEN QUESTIONS: Should a shadow root that only slots a light-DOM target count as \"enclosing\" and be hidden around it? The orchestrator needs to decide the target-subtree semantics for bug 1 (is everything under a target visible, including shadow siblings?)."
